sub_0203FEF4 / sub_020401F0: BOOL native-script callbacks that fall off the
end (no return statement). On the ROM the value returned is r0 as the last
call left it (scrcmd_3.o: `bl sub_02082158; pop {r4, pc}`), i.e. the callee's
own BOOL (sub_02082158 / sub_02081EB8 -> sub_02081EC0 both return 0/1,
arm9/asm/unk_02080C38.s), and the script engine keeps waiting while it is
FALSE. In wasm a missing return is an undefined value, so the callbacks
return the callee's result explicitly, and the two prototypes say BOOL,
which is what the assembly returns.

